# ArduPlane parameters for the c172x, layered over ArduPilot's Tools/autotest/models/plane.parm:
#   sim_vehicle.py -v ArduPlane --model JSON:<host> --add-param-file Tools/autotest/models/plane.parm --add-param-file <this file>
# plane.parm is written for a small RC plane (cruise 22 m/s, minimum 10 m/s); a 172 stalls above that.
# The simulator's airspeed sensor arrives in the JSON "airspeed" field, which only the SITL sensor type reads.
ARSPD_TYPE 100
ARSPD_USE 1
# AIRSPEED_MIN is TECS's underspeed floor: at or below it TECS demands PTCH_LIM_MIN, and on the runway that pins the
# nose down at rotation speed and the aircraft swings on its nosewheel (measured: nav_pitch -15 from 27 m/s with
# the POH's 28). The JSBSim c172x lifts off and climbs at 25 m/s, so the floor sits under that; cruise and maximum
# follow the POH (Vy 75 KIAS, Vno 128 KIAS).
AIRSPEED_MIN 22
AIRSPEED_CRUISE 38
AIRSPEED_MAX 60
# Rotate where the wing flies: held level past 28 m/s the c172x wheelbarrows on its nosewheel and swings; PX4's
# airframe rotates at 18 m/s for the same reason. 2 deg is its stance, so the roll is elevator-neutral.
TKOFF_ROTATE_SPD 25
TKOFF_GND_PITCH 2
# Ground steering only exists below this height (ArduPlane Attitude.cpp, stabilize_yaw); at the default 0 the
# runway roll is steered by the coordinated-turn rudder, which follows a swing instead of holding the course.
GROUND_STEER_ALT 5
# JSBSim's c172x (propeller sense -1, p_factor 10) yaws right under power: hands off it turned 40 deg during the
# take-off roll (measured in MANUAL), and at lift-off alpha the p-factor takes about half the rudder. ArduPlane's
# rudder only coordinates turns by default; its yaw controller puts out DAMP * (integrator - yaw rate) degrees,
# so the damping gain sizes the whole output and the sideslip/integrator gains set how fast it trims the p-factor.
# SLIP/INT 1.5 hunted on final (heading 259-277 with an 8 s period, measured); halved.
YAW2SRV_DAMP 1.0
YAW2SRV_SLIP 1.0
YAW2SRV_INT 0.7
YAW2SRV_IMAX 3000
TKOFF_THR_MAX 100
TKOFF_ALT 80
TKOFF_LVL_PITCH 5
# JSBSim c172x measured: full-throttle climb 3.5 m/s, idle sink about 4 m/s.
TECS_CLMB_MAX 3.5
TECS_SINK_MIN 3
TECS_SINK_MAX 5
PTCH_LIM_MAX_DEG 12
PTCH_LIM_MIN_DEG -10
ROLL_LIMIT_DEG 25
LEVEL_ROLL_LIMIT 5
TRIM_THROTTLE 60
# A one-tonne aircraft at 38 m/s: the default 60 m loiter would need a 68 deg bank (400 m: 20 deg), and the
# default L1 period is for a small RC plane that rolls in a fraction of a second.
WP_LOITER_RAD 400
WP_RADIUS 90
NAVL1_PERIOD 25
RLL2SRV_TCONST 0.5
PTCH2SRV_TCONST 0.5
# plane.parm's rate loops are the Rascal's: with them a 5 deg pitch demand overshot to 16 deg on 9 % elevator
# (full power pitches the c172x up), and a 27 deg bank came back at 5 deg/s on 30 % aileron. Starting point for
# AUTOTUNE: three times the Rascal's gains.
PTCH_RATE_P 0.5
PTCH_RATE_I 0.3
PTCH_RATE_D 0.02
PTCH_RATE_FF 1.0
RLL_RATE_P 0.6
RLL_RATE_I 0.3
RLL_RATE_D 0.02
RLL_RATE_FF 0.5
# Measured with the defaults: TECS swung the pitch demand between its limits with a 16 s period and the height
# by 70 m, and the pitch overshot the demand by 7 deg. Slower height loop, more damping, capped rates.
TECS_TIME_CONST 15
TECS_PTCH_DAMP 1.0
TECS_THR_DAMP 0.7
TECS_INTEG_GAIN 0.1
TECS_VERT_ACC 3
THR_SLEWRATE 30
PTCH2SRV_RMAX_UP 30
PTCH2SRV_RMAX_DN 30
RLL2SRV_RMAX 60
# Take-off mode holds the wings level until TKOFF_LVL_ALT or TKOFF_DIST from the start, whichever comes first, then
# navigates to the loiter point TKOFF_DIST ahead. The c172x rolls about 500 m before it lifts off, so at the default
# distance the level phase ended at lift-off and the navigation asked for a 25 deg bank at 13 m (measured).
TKOFF_DIST 1500
TKOFF_LVL_ALT 40
# Landing: flaps 30 (full); 29 m/s is 56 KIAS, under the POH's 60-70 because without brakes the idle roll-out
# from 28 m/s ran 980 m on a 650 m runway (measured) and roll-out length goes with the square of touchdown speed. Without flaps the c172x floated 550 m past the aim point at
# 32 m/s (measured); the Rascal's 1 deg flare attitude would land a 172 on its nosewheel. Flaps are output 5 of
# the ArduPilot bindings (Controls.xml); FlapAuto (3) applies the landing and take-off percentages.
SERVO5_FUNCTION 3
LAND_FLAP_PERCNT 100
FLAP_SLEWRATE 10
TECS_LAND_ARSPD 29
LAND_PITCH_DEG 5
LAND_FLARE_ALT 3
LAND_FLARE_SEC 2
LAND_DISARMDELAY 10
